# Deploys run from the REPO ROOT (the Vercel project's Root Directory is "frontend").
#
# Without this file the CLI uploaded essentially the entire working directory --
# measured at 2612 files against 2633 present on disk, of which 2294 were gitignored.
# .gitignore is NOT a reliable filter for the upload; this file is. That is how a
# previous local build (frontend/dist) reached the build context, and Tailwind v4 --
# which auto-detects its sources by walking the project -- scanned that stale bundle
# and harvested class-like tokens out of it, emitting 14 utilities nothing uses plus
# their !important variants: +2.5kB, and production CSS no longer reproducible from a
# clean checkout.
#
# So: anything that must stay out of the upload belongs HERE, not only in .gitignore.
frontend/dist
frontend/node_modules
frontend/coverage

# The .NET half of the repo, which the frontend build never reads. This is the bulk of
# it -- 2043 of the excluded files were bin/ and obj/ compiler output.
#
# Every pattern below MUST stay anchored with a leading slash. These follow .gitignore
# matching, so a bare "src" matches a directory of that name at ANY depth -- it takes
# frontend/src with it, and the build dies on "TS18003: No inputs were found in config
# file tsconfig.app.json". Anchored, they match only the repo root. Note these two
# lines are also what currently keeps bin/obj out; do not drop them casually.
/src
/tests
/AltitudELog.slnx
/Directory.Build.props
/Dockerfile
/docker-compose.yml
